00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.280
<b>Crow Castle, Bizen</b>

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.820
Isn't it done yet?

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:06.520
It takes forever for the daikon to cook all the way through... {he's saying in general}

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:09.490
Kingo. {this is anickname supposedly}

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:14.040
I-Ieyasu-san?! Why are you here?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:15.160
Don't get any closer!

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:17.260
No one is going to yell at you. {is it semeru as in attack or scold?*}{dunno, could be either really}

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.670
Don't be afraid.

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:23.980
But if Mouri-sama or Mitsunari-kun found out you were here, I'd get in big trouble!

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:28.880
Kingo, that's exactly why I want to form a bond with you.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.570
As a fellow man.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.630
As a fellow man? {wtf why is he blushing}

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.620
<i>Kingo, know your place.</i>

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:39.080
<i>Don't irritate me, Kingo.</i>

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:44.830
But if I betray Mouri-sama or Mitsunari-kun...

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.820
I'll wait for your favorable reply, Kingo.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.650
Let's meet again.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.760
What should I do?

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.920
But-but-but-but-but-but...

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.250
It's all right, Kingo-san.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.090
You should do what <i>you</i> want to do.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:10.900
T-Tenkai-sama!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.620
<i>The fact that Tokugawa Ieyasu visited Kobayakawa Hideaki</i>

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:17.030
<i>was soon transmitted to Osaka.</i>

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:20.180
What? Ieyasu went to Kingo?

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:24.260
For now, it appears that Tokugawa is one step ahead of us.  {It looks like Tokugawa got one up on us.} {I like the phrase but its probably too informal for Gyoubu}{Not sure if there is a more formal way to say this?}

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:26.920
Damn you, Ieyasu!

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:30.200
We should make a move as well.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.320
<i>The Saika village.</i>

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:38.850
<i>After unexpectedly forming a contract with the Saika brigade, Maeda Keiji still remained in the village.</i>

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:41.900
<i>The search was underway for his aunt Matsu, who had been kidnapped.</i>

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.300
It's really comin' down.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.380
Is Tsuruhime-chan still not back yet?

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.220
She suddenly ran off, saying she was going to meet with Tokugawa.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:51.360
Is that so?

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:54.700
You've really got a lot of reports there. {That is really a lot of reports you have there.}

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:57.610
Information gathering is another one of our specialties.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.680
Our battles are decided before they even begin.

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:01.990
Oh, I see.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.390
So, was there anything on Matsu-neechan?

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.180
Unfortunately, not yet.

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:08.280
I see...

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.220
What is it?

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.820
There's some strange movements from Kobayakawa's troops.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:16.260
From Kobayakawa?

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:21.620
For some reason, he's dispatched small
 groups of his soldiers all over the country.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.730
Gathering information?

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:24.960
Or...

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:32.050
<i>At that time, Ishida Mitsunari, Ootani Yoshitsugu, and 
Mouri Motonari were heading to see Kobayakawa Hideaki.</i>

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.560
Let me go, Mitsunari-kun!

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.080
Did you or did you not meet with Ieyasu?!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:39.860
I-I...

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.520
I won't forgive dishonesty! {lies!}

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.830
I met him! I did!

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:47.100
And did you form an agreement to betray Hideyoshi-sama?

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.210
Answer me!

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:49.960
O-Of course not!

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.280
I didn't invite Ieyasu! He just came!

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:55.080
It's true!

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.550
Looking at you makes me sick. {is unpleasant.} {check}

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:58.770
I'm sorry—

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:01.340
I won't forgive betrayal!

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:03.720
Stop!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.760
The moment you betray me, your head will fly!

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:13.110
Have you nothing to add, comrade?

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.590
I expect nothing of Kingo.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:17.690
I will leave it to the Dark King.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:20.680
I came here to see someone else.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.470
You should come as well.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.390
Mouri-dono, Gyoubu-dono.

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:30.510
I am extremely honored that you 
would come all the way here to visit me.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.250
Who are you?

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.960
For what purpose are you manipulating Kingo?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.090
Please do not accuse me of such things.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:40.180
I am simply Kingo-san's advisor.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:44.540
And Kingo-san has not betrayed you.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.810
He is an honest man.

00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:49.530
Who would believe such nonsense?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.270
I have proof that we are your ally.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:53.400
Proof?

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:57.010
Here.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:02.370
The wife of Maeda Toshiie of Kaga province,

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:03.780
Matsu-dono.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.280
Matsu

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.420
What is the meaning of this?

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:08.980
I kidnapped her.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:12.290
Of course, I made it seem as if it were done by Ieyasu. {an act of Ieyasu's. {check k}

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:17.290
I think it would be beneficial to make the Maeda family our allies.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.010
What an amusing diversion. {check}{興 entertainment? isn't it 強要}{~yo no is just the end of the sentence so it has to be like "kyou"}

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:32.660
What bad taste. {or: It's quite tasteless. whichi sbetter}{Perhaps 'What bad taste you have...'?}{it has to follow up the rpevious "It's amusing" No, it's in bad taste}{"You certainly lack taste..." ?}

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:36.480
But at least you understand that we are still allies.{that we have not changed our intentions towards you}

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.440
In other words, you are asking us to include you in our strategies

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.610
If you do, then I will surely be of use to you.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.650
Fine, we will include you.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.640
Do you believe him?

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:55.240
In this world of war, what can anyone believe in?

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.630
But we can make use of him.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.490
I hope so.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:04.100
I smell the stench of ruin on him.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.500
Do as you like.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.500
A guest will arrive for us shortly.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.640
Let's return.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:15.730
OSAKA  CASTLE{changed this font to look more more agressive like the sign}

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:19.920
That's Kasuga for you.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.400
Stop chatting!

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.130
Sorry I made you come with me.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.240
I didn't come here for you.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:27.580
I'm here on Kenshin-sama's orders.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.480
Takeda's monkeys?

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.160
I've been waiting for you.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.220
Does nothing surprise you?

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:41.160
So, do you wanna form an alliance with us?

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:45.840
We can't exactly afford to support a sick tiger.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.570
But if you surrender to us, we'll consider it. {check}{ok}

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:51.420
Of course you have your doubts.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:54.140
But I can't have you underestimating the Takeda like that.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.090
We're quite cautious, you know.

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:59.650
Let's play a little and see how you do.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:03.800
Mitsunari!

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:06.620
Tokugawa's spies have infiltrated the castle!

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:07.700
That's dirty!

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:16.070
Are you all right, Gyoubu?

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:17.410
Those are the spies.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.920
Ieyasu's ninjas?

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.450
This is <i>your</i> job.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.420
...Right.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:32.160
I won't allow Ieyasu's followers to invade Hideyoshi-sama's castle! {check}{"anyone associated with Ieyasu" / "Ieysu's minions"? 息がかかったもの}

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.000
Throw me a bone, here?

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.000
Do you need one?

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:41.900
Can't you tell? {check}{k}

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:50.410
You guys are Ieyasu's allies?

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:53.260
Sorry, it looks like I can't help you out.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:55.080
Well, that sucks.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.670
Repent your ignorance and die!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:11.610
"Elegant" fights just aren't my style, ya know.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:20.910
Oh? Going on the defensive already?

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.350
You're one to talk!

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:35.200
Stop right there!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.190
Hey! You filthy little rats! {Hey! Don't do something so impudent.} {I dot like this word for him}{i don't rly like impudent either. sth like "you dirty little rats" maybe}

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:43.430
What are you after, minions of Ieyasu? {is that right}{can't hear the last word **}

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:47.620
Unfortunately, we're not from Tokugawa, Dark King.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:48.460
What?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:51.410
These are Takeda's monkeys.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:55.220
If there's a monkey here tonight, it's <i>you</i>, Ootani. {check}

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:58.220
Takeda...?

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:04.010
No matter who you are, I will slice up anyone who violates Hideyoshi-sama's castle. {ceck}

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:05.640
Wait, Mitsunari.

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:09.180
They are Tokugawa's enemies.

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:12.610
But he wants them.

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:20.160
To make him suffer and die as cruelly as possible, 
we must first steal what he wants from him.

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:22.250
What are you suggesting?

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:24.360
Will you meet with our general?

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:29.640
The Takeda want an alliance with you, Dark King.

